  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO2_NetworkServices_Q05
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: What does a reverse lookup zone actually do?
  choices:
  - Resolves an IP address back to a host name
  - Reverses the order of DNS server priority
  - Restores DNS records after a failure
  - Resolves a host name to an IP address
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  points: 10
  explanation: Forward resolves name to address. Reverse does the opposite, which
    is what a log entry or a diagnostic tool needs when all it has is the address.
